{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: derive `_busyLineRe` from the parsed manifest instead of hand-copying the face alternation**

The face alternation `^(>_o|-_-|o_o|>_<|o_<|◕‿◕|¬_¬|o_o\?|\^\.\^|-_/)  ?` now exists in 4 hand-maintained places: the `busy_row` rule, both `not`-gates in `docs/integrations/herdr/fa.toml`, and this `_busyLineRe`. `fa_tui_kaomoji_test.dart` already proves the faces can be extracted from the manifest with a one-line regex (`line_regex = \['(.+?)', ` on the `busy_row` block), and this test already parses the manifest into `_Manifest` — so this contract regex can track the manifest instead of being a second source of truth:

```dart
final busyRule = manifest.rules.firstWhere((r) => r.id == 'busy_row');
final _busyLineRe = RegExp(/* busyRule line_regex[0] */);
```

A face-set change would then only need the manifest + `kKaomojiFaces` (already cross-tested), not a third synchronized copy. Pre-existing shape (the braille regex had the same duplication), so follow-up polish — not merge-blocking.
