{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: `kaomojiPick: kaomojiPick` in `copyWith` is load-bearing but easy to misread**

`copyWith` has no `kaomojiPick` parameter, so this line re-supplies the FIELD (`this.kaomojiPick`) into the constructor. That is essential — without it every `copyWith` would silently reset an injected test picker back to the random `_defaultKaomojiPick` — but a reader can easily parse it as a parameter self-reference and "simplify" it away, which would only surface as flaky randomness in tests.

Worth one line of dartdoc on the copyWith parameter list (or on this line), e.g.:

```dart
// copyWith cannot override the picker seam; this re-supplies the field so
// an injected kaomojiPick survives every copy (dropping it would reset
// deterministic tests to the random default).
kaomojiPick: kaomojiPick,
```
